# A wide, flowing airfield sprint with three graduated runway jumps.
# Distances are metres; angles are degrees. Jumps reward a straight approach.
name "Airfield Run"
description "Three runway jumps, a banked taxiway sweep, and a raised service bridge."
width 16
start 0 0 0

# Runway one: build speed on the opening straight before a gentle launch.
# The 14 m gap lands 2.5 m below its lip, back at runway elevation.
straight 190
ramp 24 rise 2.5
gap 14 rise -2.5
straight 105
checkpoint

# A broad taxiway bend narrows the road, then opens onto runway two.
# Remove the bank well before launch so the car leaves a level road cross-section.
width 14
right 50 radius 120 bank -7
width 18
straight 80 bank 0

# Runway two: a slightly taller ramp crosses a wider break in the tarmac.
# A full 100 m of solid landing road precedes the next corner and checkpoint.
ramp 24 rise 3
gap 16 rise -3
straight 100
checkpoint

# Climb the service-road sweep, then cross a narrower elevated bridge.
# Width blends over the climb; the bridge eases the banking back to level.
width 12
left 70 radius 110 rise 4 bank 8
bridge 100 rise 4 bank 0
width 18
straight 90

# Runway three: a longer ramp and the widest gap, with a generous flat landing.
# This jump stays at the bridge's elevated level; descend only after touchdown.
ramp 28 rise 3
gap 18 rise -3
straight 110
checkpoint

# A final gentle turn descends to the main runway and a long finish straight.
width 16
right 30 radius 140 rise -4 bank -6
straight 170 rise -4 bank 0
finish
